<%# Never restored from Turbo's page cache (final fix wave 1, ledger m1): a
    snapshot of an editor holds its forms as they stood when it was left --
    typed text whose save was only sent as the page was torn down (Back
    drains nothing), next to the base from before that save. Restored, the
    form took that text for what the server holds and sent the next edit on
    the old base: refused as "Changed elsewhere" against one's own save. With
    this, Back/Forward to an editor fetches it afresh. (A frame navigation's
    answer carries the tag too, and the promoted visit merges it into the
    head, so it also holds for an editor opened from the tree.)

    And no link is prefetched from an editor (follow-up N1): Turbo fetches a
    link on hover and reuses that answer for the click. From an editor the
    click first waits for the save queue (`saving/queue.js`), so a
    prefetched answer for the same record -- its other language tab, its own
    row in the tree -- shows it as it was BEFORE those saves, with the old
    base: the saved text missing and the next edit refused. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
  <meta name="turbo-prefetch" content="false">
<% end %>

<%# The post's open notes (notes spec §4.3): two queries for the drawer's
    counts and whether they hold something unread for the viewer. Here in the
    view, because every way this screen is rendered needs them. The header's
    Notes button is a slot component (`Admin::Slots`) and is handed the same
    counts rather than reading them again. %>
<% note_counts = Notes::Counts.for_container(@post, user: Current.user) %>

<%= render Admin::EditorScreen::PostFormComponent.new(post: @post, locale: admin_locale, url_options: admin_url_options, slot_context: { counts: note_counts }) %>

<%# The notes drawer (notes spec §4.1): once per screen, after everything
    else and outside every form -- the post's form above is closed. `?notes=open`
    (a link from the inbox, the posts list) opens it on load, at `?thread=`
    when there is one. %>
<%= render Admin::NotesScreen::DrawerComponent.new(container: @post, counts: note_counts,
      title: Locales.read(@post, :title, locale: admin_locale).presence || t("admin.components.notes_screen.drawer.untitled"),
      open: params[:notes] == "open", thread: params[:thread], url_options: admin_url_options) %>
